              "reason": "The before source has the same int-valued compression bound. For 1,073,741,824 post-seed bytes, the old harness doubles a result of 1,077,952,592 in int arithmetic.",
              "source_evidence": [
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-21afc9bac77407fcdd32d654",
                  "quote": "#define LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE        0x7E000000   /* 2 113 929 216 bytes */\n#define LZ4_COMPRESSBOUND(isize)  ((unsigned)(isize) > (unsigned)LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE ? 0 : (isize) + ((isize)/255) + 16)\n\n/*! LZ4_compressBound() :\n    Provides the maximum size that LZ4 compression may output in a \"worst case\" scenario (input data not compressible)\n    This function is primarily useful for memory allocation purposes (destination buffer size).\n    Macro LZ4_COMPRESSBOUND() is also provided for compilation-time evaluation (stack memory allocation for example).\n    Note that LZ4_compress_default() compresses faster when dstCapacity is >= LZ4_compressBound(srcSize)\n        inputSize  : max supported value is LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE\n        return : maximum output size in a \"worst case\" scenario\n              or 0, if input size is incorrect (too large or negative)\n*/\nLZ4LIB_API int LZ4_compressBound(int inputSize);\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-a69e113e8f0f47c740efaf02",
                  "quote": "int LZ4_compressBound(int isize)  { return LZ4_COMPRESSBOUND(isize); }\n"
                }
              ]
            },
            "after": {
              "requirement": "Compute the compressed buffer allocation size without signed integer overflow for a library-supported input size.",
              "applicability": "required",
              "harness_status": "unsat",
              "reason": "The after source retains the same bound and int return type; the fixed old harness still overflows at the same allocation expression.",
              "source_evidence": [
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-8ed7bbb959dcde00fcc26f29",
                  "quote": "#define LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE        0x7E000000   /* 2 113 929 216 bytes */\n#define LZ4_COMPRESSBOUND(isize)  ((unsigned)(isize) > (unsigned)LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE ? 0 : (isize) + ((isize)/255) + 16)\n\n/*! LZ4_compressBound() :\n    Provides the maximum size that LZ4 compression may output in a \"worst case\" scenario (input data not compressible)\n    This function is primarily useful for memory allocation purposes (destination buffer size).\n    Macro LZ4_COMPRESSBOUND() is also provided for compilation-time evaluation (stack memory allocation for example).\n    Note that LZ4_compress_default() compresses faster when dstCapacity is >= LZ4_compressBound(srcSize)\n        inputSize  : max supported value is LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE\n        return : maximum output size in a \"worst case\" scenario\n              or 0, if input size is incorrect (too large or negative)\n*/\nLZ4LIB_API int LZ4_compressBound(int inputSize);\n"
